course: dictionary
lesson: 15343
title: Sojourn: a short stay
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sojourn is a short stay in a place that is not your home. It is a formal word, so you will find it in travel writing, older books and exam texts. «We are going on a short sojourn by the sea.» The clues are short, by the sea and not home. The family is visiting for a while, not moving there for good.
explain: When you meet an unknown word, ask what word would fit in its place. In «We are going on a short sojourn by the sea», the word stay fits. Try it: «We are going on a short stay by the sea» still makes sense, so sojourn means a stay.
explain: Sojourn can also be a verb. To sojourn means to stay somewhere for a while as a visitor. «They sojourned in Rome for a week.» In the Bible, Abraham sojourned in a land as a stranger, which means he lived there as a traveller, not as a native.
fact: A sojourn is a short stay in a place that is not your home.
fact: Sojourn is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in books, travel writing and exams.
fact: In everyday talk, people say stay or visit instead of sojourn.
fact: To sojourn means to stay somewhere for a while as a visitor, and it is often used in old-fashioned writing.
fact: In the Bible, to sojourn means to live in a land as a stranger or traveller, as Abraham did.
exercise: «The family enjoyed a brief sojourn in the mountains.» What does sojourn mean here? | *A short stay away from home | A long move into a new house | A race up a steep hill | A school trip to a museum
exercise: «They sojourned in Rome for a week before flying home.» What does sojourned mean? | Built a new house | *Stayed somewhere for a while as a visitor | Packed their bags and left forever | Ran away for good
exercise: «Our sojourn in the village was short, but we loved it.» Find and copy the word that means a stay in a place that is not home. | short | *sojourn | loved | village
test: «During our sojourn in Wales, we stayed in a tiny cottage.» What is a simpler word for sojourn here? | Garage | *Stay | Homework | Race
test: In the Bible, Abraham sojourned in a foreign land. What does sojourned mean here? | He was born there and always lived there | He built a city and never left | He ruled the land as its king | *He lived there as a stranger or traveller
exam: «The students' sojourn in the old town was brief, but it changed how they saw history.» Which explanation best fits sojourn? | A long job teaching in a school | *A short stay in a place that is not home | A quick sprint across a field | A lesson about history in class
